# Qdat Command Flow

### Version Number

```apl 
*VERSION 

```


### Unit System (Note: Currently only supports N, M import)

```apl 
*UNIT    

```


### Creep Function

```apl 
*CREEPFCT     
;Name=Name, Scaling Coefficient
;Time1, Creep Coefficient1...
```


### Shrink Function

```apl 
*SHRINKFCT     
;Name=Name, Scaling Coefficient
;Time1, Shrink Strain1...
```


### Creep and Shrink

```apl 
*TDMATERIAL     
;Material Number, Name, Code Number (Note: 1-Highway Code 2018), Humidity, Cement Type Coefficient, Shrink Start Age, Fly Ash Content Percentage
;Material Number, Name, Code Number (Note: 2-Highway Code 2004), Humidity, Cement Type Coefficient, Shrink Start Age
;Material Number, Name, Code Number (Note: 3-Highway Code 85), Creep Basic Coefficient, Creep Calculation Parameter, Shrink Speed Coefficient, Shrink Ultimate Value
;Material Number, Name, Code Number (Note: 4-Railway Code 17), Humidity, Creep Basic Coefficient, Creep Calculation Parameter, Shrink Speed Coefficient, Shrink Ultimate Value
;Material Number, Name, Code Number (Note: 5-Metro Design Code), Humidity, Shrink Speed Coefficient, Shrink Ultimate Value
;Material Number, Name, Code Number (Note: 6-Aging Theory), Creep Ultimate Value, Creep Growth Speed, Shrink Speed Coefficient, Shrink Ultimate Value
;Material Number, Name, Code Number (Note: 7-BS5400), Humidity, Cement Content, Water-Cement Ratio, Concrete Type
;Material Number, Name, Code Number (Note: 8-AASHTO), Humidity, Curing Days
;Material Number, Name, Code Number (Note: 1000-User Defined), Shrink Function Name, Creep Function Name1, Loading Age1...
```


### Material Detailed Information

```apl 
*MAT-INFO       
;Material Number, Name, Type (Note: 1-Concrete), Code Number, Database, Construction Coefficient, Creep Material Number (Note: -1 means no creep and shrink), Modify (Note: YES/NO), Modulus of Elasticity, Unit Weight, Poisson's Ratio, Expansion Coefficient
;Material Number, Name, Type (Note: 2-Steel), Code Number, Database, Construction Coefficient, Modify (YES/NO), Modulus of Elasticity, Unit Weight, Poisson's Ratio, Expansion Coefficient
;Material Number, Name, Type (Note: 3-Prestressing/Steel Wire), Code Number, Database (Note: includes plate thickness suffix as (t1_t2)), Construction Coefficient, Modify (Note: YES/NO), Modulus of Elasticity, Unit Weight, Poisson's Ratio, Expansion Coefficient
;Material Number, Name, Type (Note: 4-Reinforcement), Code Number, Database, Construction Coefficient (default is 1), Modify (YES/NO), Modulus of Elasticity, Unit Weight, Poisson's Ratio, Expansion Coefficient
;Material Number, Name, Type (Note: 5-Custom), Construction Coefficient, Modulus of Elasticity, Unit Weight, Poisson's Ratio, Expansion Coefficient, Creep Material Number (Note: -1 means no creep and shrink), Fcuk
;Material Number, Name, Type (Note: 6-Composite Material), Main Material Name, Auxiliary Material Name
```


### Section Detailed Information

```apl 
*SEC-INFO    
;ID=Section Number, Name, Type-Single Section, Consider Shear (YES/NO),(Eccentricity Y-Relative to Centroid, Eccentricity Z-Relative to Centroid)/(Centroid/Geometric Center, Alignment Point)
;W,H   ;Rectangular Section and other general parameter sections (refer to section table order)
;B,N,H,YES/NO    ;Concrete Box Girder Overall Data
;H1,H2,H2a,H2b,B1,B1a,B1b,B2,B3,B4,T1,T2,T3,T4,,R1,R2   ;Concrete Box Girder Cell Data 1
;C1(a1,b1,a2,b2...),C3(a1,b1,a2,b2...),C2(a1,b1,a2,b2...),C4(a1,b1,a2,b2...)   ;Concrete Box Girder Left Box Web Top and Bottom Fillet Data 1
;Li1/LB0/LB4/LT4 =a1,a2,a3...  ;Concrete Box Girder Left Box List Data (not output when single data)
;Ri1/RB0/RB4/RT4 =a1,a2,a3...  ;Concrete Box Girder Right Box List Data (not output when single data)
;topDis,botDis,B1,B2,B3,B4,H,t1,t2,tw   ;I-Section Steel Beam Basic Data
;topDis,botDis,B1,B2,B3,B4,B5,B6,H,t1,t2,tw1,tw2   ;Box Section Steel Beam Basic Data
;Symmetric (0-Symmetric 1-Asymmetric),boxNum,type(0-General),Direction(0-Left 1-Right),B1,B2,B3,B4,B5,B6,Br1,Br2,Br3,Br4,Br5,H,tf1,tf2,tw1,tw2   ;Single Box Multi-Cell Steel Beam General Section
;Symmetric (0-Symmetric 1-Asymetric),boxNum,type(1-Strengthening 1),Direction(0-Left 1-Right),B1,B2,B3,B4,B5,B6,Br1,Br2,Br3,Br4,Br5,H,tf1,tf2,tw1,tw2,rh,rt,rb,rtr,rbr,rt1r,rt2r,h1r,h2r,h3r,rbr,rt1r,rt2r   ;Single Box Multi-Cell Steel Beam Strengthening 1 Type Section
;Symmetric (0-Symmetric 1-Asymetric),boxNum,type(2-Strengthening 2),Direction(0-Left 1-Right),B1,B2,B3,B4,B5,B6,Br1,Br2,Br3,Br4,Br5,H,tf1,tf2,tw1,tw2,rh1,rh2,rh3,rb,rt1r,rt2r,h1r,h2r,h3r,rbr,rt1r,rt2r   ;Single Box Multi-Cell Steel Beam Strengthening 2 Type Section
;Es/Ec,Ds/Dc,Ps,Pc,Ts/Tc   ;Composite Beam Section Material Properties
;Ax,Ay,Az,Ix,Iy,Iz,Iyz,Cyp,Cym,Czp,Czm,PeriO,PeriI,CentY,CentZ,Y1,Z1,Y2,Z2,Y3,Z3,Y4,Z4,ShearY,ShearZ,Thw   ;Custom Properties Section Information
;RIB=Rib Name,H,B/(T Rib when parameters are H,B,tw,tf)/(U Rib when parameters are H,B1,B2,t,R)   ;Steel Beam Plate Rib Data
;PLACE=Layout Position (I-Section Steel Beam 1-5, Steel Section Box Girder 1-8 Upper Left is 1 and others follow),Reference Point 0-1,Spacing,Rib Name,Stiffening Rib Position (0-2),Stiffening Rib Name    ;Steel Beam Plate Rib Layout Data
;MAIN=(x1,y1),(x2,y2)...  ;Custom Wire Loop Section Outer Loop Information
;SUB=(x1,y1),(x2,y2)...  ;Custom Wire Loop Section Inner Loop Information
;LINE=x1,y1,x2,y2,t...   ;Custom Line Width Section Information
;ID=Section Number, Name, Type-Variable Section, Consider Shear (YES/NO),Eccentricity Information I (Refer to Single Section),Eccentricity Information J (Refer to Single Section)
;I/J=   ;Variable Section IJ/J End Data Identifier Line, subsequent data is consistent with Single Section data
;M/S=   ;Custom Composite Section Main and Auxiliary Data Identifier Line, subsequent data is consistent with Custom Wire Loop data
```


### Node Information

```apl 
*NODE   
;Node Number, Coordinate X, Coordinate Y, Coordinate Z
```


### Element Information

```apl 
*ELEMENT    
;Number, Type (Note: 1-Beam 2-Truss), Material Number, Section Number, Beta Angle, Node I, Node J
;Number, Type (Note: 3-Cable), Material Number, Section Number, Beta Angle, Node I, Node J, Tensioning Type (Note: 1-Initial Tension Force 2-Initial Horizontal Force 3-Unstressed Length), Tension Value
;Number, Type (Note: 4-Plate), Material Number, Section Number, Beta Angle, Node I, Node J, Node K, Node L, Plate Element Type (1-Thick Plate 0-Thin Plate)
```


### Variable Section Group

```apl 
*TSGROUP    
;Name, Element Set (Note: XtoYbyN), Width Direction Power Exponent, Width Direction Reference Point, Width Direction Distance, Height Direction Power Exponent, Height Direction Reference Point, Height Direction Distance
```


### Thickness

```apl 
*THICKNESS      
;THICK=Id, Name, Thickness, Consider Eccentricity (YES/NO), Eccentricity Type (Note: 0-Thickness Ratio 1-Value), Eccentricity Value      ;General Plate Thickness
;THICK=Id, Name, Thickness, Rib Plate Position (Note: 0-Bottom 1-Top)      ;Stiffening Rib Plate Thickness
;HasRib (Note: YES/NO), Spacing, Rib Plate Type, H,B,Tw,Tf      ;Longitudinal Section Rib Information
;HasRib (Note: YES/NO), Spacing, Rib Plate Type, H,B,Tw,Tf      ;Transverse Section Rib Information
;For U-type Plate, parameters are -H,B1,B2,T,R      ;U-type Plate Section Rib Information
```


### Structure Group

```apl 
*STRGROUP   
;Name, Node Set (Note: XtoYbyN), Element Set (Note: XtoYbyN)
```


### Boundary Group

```apl 
*BNDRGROUP  
;Boundary Group Name 1, Boundary Group Name 2...
```


### General Support

```apl 
*GSUPPORT       
;Node Number, Constraint Information (Note: DxyzRxyz 0-free 1-fixed), Group Name
```


### Elastic Support

```apl 
*ESUPPORT   
;Node Number, Type (Note: 1-LINE 2-TENS 3-COMP), Group Name, kx,ky,kz,krx,kry,krz
;Node Number, Type (Note: 2-TENS 3-COMP), Group Name, Direction (0-x 1-negative x 2-y 3-negative y 4-z 5-negative z), kx
```


### Elastic Link

```apl 
*ELINK      
;Type (GEN-General x), Node Number I, Node Number J, Beta, Boundary Group Name, KDx,KDy,KDz,kRx,KRy,KRz, Distance Ratio
;Type (RIGID-Rigid), Node Number I, Node Number J, Beta, Boundary Group Name
;Type (TENS-Tension COMP-Compression), Node Number I, Node Number J, Beta, Boundary Group Name, Kx
```


### Master-Slave Constraint

```apl 
*MSLINK     
;Master Node Number, Slave Node Number, Constraint Information (Note: DxyzRxyz 0-free 1-fixed), Group Name
```


### Node Coordinate System

```apl 
*LOCALAXIS      
;Node Number, V1(x,y,z), V2(x,y,z)     Note: Vector is enclosed by parentheses
```


### Beam End Restraints

```apl 
*RESTRAINTS    
;Element ID, I End Degrees of Freedom (Note: DxyzRxyz 0-free 1-fixed), J End Degrees of Freedom (Note: DxyzRxyz 0-free 1-fixed), Boundary Group
```


### Constraint Equation

```apl 
*EQUATION      
;Name, Group Name, Slave Node Number, Slave Node Degrees of Freedom, Master Node Information (Master Node Number 1, Degrees of Freedom, Scale Factor)
```


